        "description": "autoEstCont heterogeneous-cell assumption: The source describes a scientific assumption and likely failures, not a universal execution block. Frozen core lacks an assumption/limitation predicate; do not turn this into unconditional REQUIRED or SAFE_BLOCKING.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "content_hash": "29de98ee91160ea0440d91a61d2ac1024a8e2c00f1dc58ae2c53503b16286625",
            "end_offset": 12111,
            "evidence_span_id": "evidence-span:58bdf7d1ac531a193aa27369",
            "exact_text": "This function assumes that the channel contains multiple distinct cell types with different marker\ngenes. If you try and run it on a channel with very homogenous cells (e.g. a cell line, flow-sorted\ncells), you will likely get a warning, an error, and/or an extremely high contamination estimate.\nIn such circumstances your best option is usually to manually set the contamination to something\nreasonable.",
